// The Vilij — Safeguarding Policy
// Content transcribed from "THE VILIJ Safeguarding Policy (Final).pdf",
// version 1.1, effective 24 July 2026. See content-issues.md C56.
//
// Transcribed verbatim, on the same terms as the other three solicitor
// documents: nothing corrected, renumbered, modernised or tidied. That means
// the following faults in the source are reproduced here rather than fixed, and
// are recorded in content-issues.md C62:
//
//   * §16.8 prints an item "(g)" with no text at all — just the letter and a
//     semicolon. Publishing an empty bracket would be worse than the fault, so
//     the item is omitted and (h) and (i) keep the letters the document prints.
//     That is what `itemLabels` on clause 16.8 is doing.
//   * §19.5 is a heading, "Emergency and external contacts", with no clause
//     text; the content it introduces is numbered 19.6. Reproduced as printed.
//   * §19.1 names the policy owner "Charlene Andruskeviciu"; §19.4 names the
//     same person "Charlene Andruskevicius". Both spellings are as printed.
//
// No [] or email@email.co.uk placeholders appear anywhere in this document —
// unlike the Complaints procedure (C55) and the Terms (C54), every contact
// detail in clause 19.4 is filled in. Those details include two named
// individuals' personal mobile numbers, which is a publication decision rather
// than a transcription one; it is flagged in content-issues.md C63.
